#: src/view.cpp:1953
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "You can control your paddle either with the mouse or keyboard. Destroying "
#| "bricks will release extras sometimes. Some are good, some are bad and "
#| "some may be good or bad. Some of the bricks take more than one shot, "
#| "regenerate over time, explode or grow new bricks (see README for more "
#| "details). Balls will get faster (until life is lost) and the difficulty "
#| "setting will influence number of lives, ball speed, paddle size and "
#| "score.\n"
#| "\n"
#| "While playing you can press\n"
#| "  - ESC to leave the game (you'll have to confirm)\n"
#| "  - w to warp to next level (if enough bricks were destroyed)\n"
#| "  - p to pause/unpause the game\n"
#| "  - d to destroy a brick (workaround for bad level design)\n"
#| "\n"
#| "If you leave a game you can resume it later (no hiscores entry yet).\n"
#| "\n"
#| "If you loose all lives you can buy a continue (score set to 0, initial "
#| "number of lives restored). If you don't buy a continue the game is over "
#| "(hiscores entry is checked) and can no longer be resumed. \n"
#| "\n"
#| "Enjoy the game!\n"
#| "          Michael Speck"
msgid ""
"You can control your paddle either with the mouse or keyboard. Destroying "
"bricks will release extras sometimes. Some are good, some are bad and some "
"may be good or bad. Some of the bricks take more than one shot, regenerate "
"over time, explode or grow new bricks (see README for more details). Balls "
"will get faster (until life is lost) and the difficulty setting will "
"influence number of lives, ball speed, paddle size and score.\n"
"\n"
"While playing you can press\n"
"  - ESC to leave the game (you'll have to confirm)\n"
"  - W to warp to next level (if enough bricks were destroyed)\n"
"  - P to pause/unpause the game\n"
"  - D to destroy a brick (workaround for bad level design)\n"
"\n"
"If you leave a game, you can resume it later (no hiscores entry yet).\n"
"\n"
"If you lose all lives, you can buy a continue (score set to 0, initial "
"number of lives restored). If you don't buy a continue, the game is over "
"(hiscores entry is checked) and can no longer be resumed. \n"
"\n"
"Enjoy the game!\n"
"          Michael Speck"
msgstr ""
"Der Schläger lässt sich mit Maus oder Tastatur kontrollieren. Zerstörte "
"Steine werden manchmal Extras freigeben. Manche sind gut, manche schlecht "
"und manche gut oder schlecht. Einige der Steine brauchen mehr als einen "
"Schuss, regenerieren über die Zeit, explodieren oder erzeugen neue Steine "
"(siehe README für mehr Details). Bälle werden mit der Zeit schneller und der "
"Schwierigkeitsgrad beeinflußt die Anzahl an Leben, Ballgeschwindigkeit, "
"Schlägergröße und Punktezahl.\n"
"\n"
"Es gibt folgende Sondertasten im Spiel\n"
"  - ESC  verlässt das Spiel (muss bestätigt werden)\n"
"  - w    springt in die nächste Ebene (falls genug Steine zerstört wurden)\n"
"  - p    pausiert das Spiel\n"
"  - d    erlaubt Zerstörung einzelner Steine (für schlechtes Leveldesign)\n"
"\n"
"Falls du ein Spiel beendest, kannst du es später wieder aufnehmen. Es wird "
"noch kein Eintrag in die Bestenliste erstellt. Wenn du alle Leben verlierst, "
"kannst du ein Continue kaufen (Punktzahl wird auf 0 gesetzt, die anfängliche "
"Anzahl an Leben wird wiederhergestellt). Falls du kein Continue kaufst, ist "
"das Spiel vorbei (Bestenliste wird geprüft) und kann nicht mehr aufgenommen "
"werden.\n"
"\n"
"Viel Spaß!\n"
"          Michael Speck"

